{"uid":"u0226","annotator":"Azouz","label":"correct","quote":"SUMMARY\nContext carried over from the earlier conversation:\n\n## Goal\nHelp the user with all of Csilla Bakery's writing this month: blog posts, the newsletter, press releases, product descriptions, and the ordering app's release notes.\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- Never make health claims about the products.\n- Target length is now 1,000 words (changed from 800 mid-conversation; applies going forward).\n- In the head baker's interview (interview_baker.md), keep her long sentence verbatim — it's her exact words.\n- Put a question in the headline where possible.\n\n## Progress\n- Counted words in tasting_room_post.md (502 words, 10 paragraphs).\n- Grouped 87 app commits into features, fixes, and security for release notes.\n- Found references: \"flour supply\" → Moreau (2021), Byrne (2023); \"small business\" → Schmidt (2022), Novak (2026), Teo Byrne (2022).\n- Tracked blog post draft length (456 words) and head baker interview transcript (493 words).\n- Opened/reviewed drafts: column_draft.md, feature_draft.md, team_portrait.md, workshop_recap.md.\n- Interview transcripts reviewed: delivery driver, supplier/miller, pastry chef.\n- Saved interview_baker.md with the quote preserved.\n- Confirmed magazine publication date: November issue.\n- Confirmed newsletter uses the new template with larger header; newsletter reach is ~6,000 readers.\n- Listed available images: images/market_hall/ (7 photos) and images/team/ (12 photos).\n- Simplified three sentences in section 2 of workshop_recap.md for clarity.\n\n## Key Decisions\n- Raise word target to 1,000 words for future drafts.\n- Preserve the head baker's long sentence only in her interview.\n- Use question-form headlines where feasible.\n\n## Next Steps\n- Expand drafts toward the 1,000-word target.\n- Continue drafting/editing blog posts, newsletter, press releases, product descriptions, and release notes.\n- Possibly select images from market_hall/ and team/ folders for pieces.","time":"2026-10-30T19:04:30.722Z"}
